example.paragraph:
Compute $\mathbf{v}_{2} - \mathbf{v}_{1} = \begin{bmatrix}
      1 \\
      4 \\
      {- .5}
      \end{bmatrix}$ and $\textbf{v}_{3} - \textbf{v}_{1} = ~\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      1 \\
      0
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,.$ These two points are not multiples and hence form a linearly independent set, $S\prime$. So all statements in Theorem 5 are false, and $S$ is affinely independent. Figure 2 shows $S$ and the translated set $S\prime$. Notice that $\text{Span~}S\prime$ is a plane through the origin and $\text{aff~}S$ is a parallel plane through $\textbf{v}_{1}$, $\textbf{v}_{2}$, and $\textbf{v}_{3}$. (Only a portion of each plane is shown here, of course.)

Compute $\textbf{v}_{2} - \textbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      1 \\
      4 \\
      {- .5}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,,$ $\textbf{v}_{3} - \textbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      1 \\
      0
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,,$ and $\textbf{v}_{4} - \textbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      11 \\
      {- 1}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,,$ and row reduce the matrix:

content.paragraph:
involving the homogeneous forms of the points. Row reduction of the augmented matrix $\lbrack\begin{matrix}
      {\widetilde{\textbf{v}}}_{1} & \cdots & {\widetilde{\textbf{v}}}_{k} & \widetilde{\textbf{p}}
      \end{matrix}\rbrack$ for (8) produces the barycentric coordinates of $\textbf{p}$.﻿

example.paragraph:
Let $\textbf{a} = \begin{bmatrix}
      1 \\
      7
      \end{bmatrix}$, $\textbf{b} = \begin{bmatrix}
      3 \\
      0
      \end{bmatrix}$, $\textbf{c} = \begin{bmatrix}
      9 \\
      3
      \end{bmatrix}$, and $\textbf{p} = \begin{bmatrix}
      5 \\
      3
      \end{bmatrix}$. Find the barycentric coordinates of $\textbf{p}$ determined by the affinely independent set $\left\{ \textbf{a},\textbf{b},\textbf{c} \right\}$.﻿

